paragraph:
\subsection{Observation 1: detection and behavioral validity diverge}
\label{sec:obs-divergence}
CREST rewrites Python programs with a catalogue of syntactic transformations and ships a random-forest detector and two logistic-regression detectors with released thresholds~\cite{crest2026}. We applied the full catalogue to every canonical HumanEval~\cite{chen2021humaneval} and sanitized MBPP~\cite{austin2021mbpp} reference. Of 591 attempts, 589 emit a candidate. All 589 are detector-positive under all three heads, and 15 of them fail the original test suite. Listing~\ref{lst:crest-palindrome} shows the decisive rewrite in HumanEval/10.
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python,caption={The decisive rewrite in the HumanEval/10 failure.},label={lst:crest-palindrome}]
# reference, and the catalogue without the operand-order rule
return string + string[:beginning_of_suffix][::-1]

